es anti-bot challenges) and **fetch** as a fallback for direct URL scraping.\\n\\n## Default Routing Rule\\n\\n- Primary search backend: `firecrawl`\\n- Fallback extract backend: `fetch`\\n- Do not use search engines directly when firecrawl is available\", \"name\": \"web-search-mcp-config\"}"
/var/home/charlie/workspace/skill-monitor-report.json:625:          "arguments": "{\"action\": \"patch\", \"name\": \"devops/web-search-mcp-config\", \"old_string\": \"## Step-by-Step\\n1. Inspect current Hermes MCP config:\\n   - `cat ~/.hermes/config.yaml | grep -n -A5 -B5 'firecrawl\\\\\\\\|mcp'`\\n   - Identify whether `firecrawl` is missing, disabled, or misconfigured.\\n2. Verify Firecrawl credentials:\\n   - `cat ~/.config/firecrawl-cli/credentials.json`\\n   - Expect `apiKey` and `apiUrl`; if missing, stop and report.\\n3. Verify API reachability before editing Hermes config:\\n   - `curl -s -L -H 'Authorization: Bearer ***' https://api.firecrawl.dev/v1/search -H 'Content-Type: application/json' --data '{\\\"query\\\":\\\"<query>\\\",\\\"limit\\\":1}'`\\n   - If this fails, fix network/proxy/key first; do not touch Hermes config yet.\\n4. Install `firecrawl-mcp` if missing:\\n   - Check `npm list -g firecrawl-mcp`.\\n   - If global prefix is `/usr/local`, avoid `npm i -g` as the current user.\\n   - Preferred install:\\n     - `mkdir -p ~/.npm-global && npm config set prefix ~/.npm-global`\\n     - `npm install -g firecrawl-mcp`\\n     - Verify `~/.npm-global/bin/firecrawl-mcp` exists.\\n5. Patch Hermes config:\\n   - Ensure `mcp_servers.firecrawl` is set to:\\n     - `enabled: true`\\n     - `command: /absolute/path/to/firecrawl-mcp`\\n     - `env: FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=<key>`\\n     - `env: FIRECRAWL_API_URL=https://api.firecrawl.dev`\\n   - Keep `fetch` enabled as fallback.\\n6. Reload Hermes and verify:\\n   - Use Hermes reload path or service restart appropriate to the deployment.\\n   - Re-run the API probe from step 3 through the new MCP path.\\n\\n## Hermes reload behavior\\n- After editing `~/.hermes/config.yaml`, use `hermes mcp list` and `hermes mcp test <name>` to confirm enablement and tool discovery.\\n- A failed `hermes-web-ui.service` does not mean MCP search is broken; `fetch`/`firecrawl` are independent of that unit.\\n- If `http://127.0.0.1:8648` is up but `18648` is down, prefer checking the actual serving process/ports instead of restarting the obsolete service unit.\\n\\n## Fallback policy\\n- Primary: `firecrawl_search`\\n- Secondary: `fetch`\\n- If both are unavailable, report the exact blocker from `hermes mcp test` before retrying random search pages.\", \"new_string\": \"## Step-by-Step\\n1. Inspect current Hermes MCP config:\\n   - `cat ~/.hermes/config.yaml | grep -n -A5 -B5 'firecrawl\\\\\\\\|mcp'`\\n   - Identify whether `firecrawl` is missing, disabled, or misconfigured.\\n2. Verify Firecrawl credentials:\\n   - `cat ~/.config/firecrawl-cli/credentials.json`\\n   - Expect `apiKey` and `apiUrl`; if missing, stop and report.\\n3. Verify API reachability before editing Hermes config:\\n   - `curl -s -L -H 'Authorization: Bearer ***' https://api.firecrawl.dev/v1/search -H 'Content-Type: application/json' --data '{\\\"query\\\":\\\"<query>\\\",\\\"limit\\\":1}'`\\n   - If this fails, fix network/proxy/key first; do not touch Hermes config yet.\\n4. Install `firecrawl-mcp` if missing:\\n   - Check `npm list -g firecrawl-mcp`.\\n   - If global prefix is `/usr/local`, avoid `npm i -g` as the current user.\\n   - Preferred install:\\n     - `mkdir -p ~/.npm-global && npm config set prefix ~/.npm-global`\\n     - `npm install -g firecrawl-mcp`\\n     - Verify `~/.npm-global/bin/firecrawl-mcp` exists.\\n5. Patch Hermes config:\\n   - Ensure `mcp_servers.firecrawl` is set to:\\n     - `enabled: true`\\n     - `command: /var/home/charlie/.npm-global/bin/firecrawl-mcp`\\n     - `env: FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=<key>`\\n     - `env: FIRECRAWL_API_URL=https://api.firecrawl.dev`\\n   - Keep `fetch` enabled as fallback with:\\n     - `command: /var/home/charlie/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.3/bin/mcp-fetch-server`\\n6. Reload Hermes and verify:\\n   - Use Hermes reload path or service restart appropriate to the deployment.\\n   - Re-run the API probe from step 3 through the new MCP path.\\n\\n## Hermes reload behavior\\n- After editing `~/.hermes/config.yaml`, use `hermes mcp list` and `hermes mcp test <name>` to confirm enablement and tool discovery.\\n- A failed `hermes-web-ui.service` does not mean MCP search is broken; `fetch`/`firecrawl` are independent of that unit.\\n- If `http://127.0.0.1:8648` is up but `18648` is down, prefer checking the actual serving process/ports instead of restarting the obsolete service unit.\\n\\n## Default routing rule\\n- Primary search backend: `firecrawl`\\n- Fallback extract backend: `fetch`\\n- Do not use search engines directly when firecrawl is available.\\n\\n## Fallback policy\\n- Primary: `firecrawl_search`\\n- Secondary: `fetch`\\n- If both are unavailable, report the exact blocker from `hermes mcp test` before retrying random search pages.\"}"
